elaine: Found another onboarding annoyance: the sampleapp spinner never resolves when the SDK keeps retrying 401s. Users think the app is broken.
noah: Oof. SDK should not retry on 4xx (except 429). That was our parity intention.
elaine: Repro: bad key -> repeated 401 logs.
vik: Proposal: define a normalized error envelope exported by SDKs: { name, status_code, code, message, retryable, retry_after?, user_hint, raw_body? } and provide typed classes (AuthError, RateLimitError, ClientError, ServerError, TransientError).
noah: Make `user_hint` UI-friendly copy. Also telemetry needs `error_class` tag for rollups.
elaine: Quick fix: sampleapp PR will bail on 4xx and show a login CTA. Longer term: SDK change to run token-refresh first, then classify.
vik: Migration note: keep legacy fields for backwards compat but add typed classes in minor. Add unit tests that stub 401 -> no retry and AuthError thrown.
docs-bot: Reminder: add docs snippet for error handling patterns and link to onboarding checklist.
noah: Snippet suggestion:
```js
try { await client.call() } catch (e) {
 if (e.name === 'AuthError') showRelogin();
 else if (e.name === 'RateLimitError') showRateLimit(e.retry_after);
 else if (e.retryable) retryWithBackoff();
 else showGeneric(e.user_hint || 'Try again later');
}
```
elaine: I'll open RFC + sampleapp PR. assigning @vik to review SDK parity across js/py. thanks!
